The data source is a single relational table where each row describes a conflict event. Distinct real-world entity types can be isolated as follows.

First, the event itself is a distinct entity. The column event_id_cnty is a unique alphanumeric event identifier constant per record and populated for every row, making it the best subject. It maps to the ontology class bsm:Action because the ontology explicitly states Action is used for conflict events. Properties mapped: event_type to bsm:conceptName (name evidence), notes to bsm:actionDescriptionText (description evidence: notes is a short description of the event), event_date to bsm:eventStartDateTime (name evidence), event_id_cnty also to bsm:sourceIdentifier (name evidence: primary key), actor1 and actor2 to bsm:involvedActor as IRIs referencing Actor entities, location and country to bsm:hasGeographicLocation as IRI referencing Location, and fatalities via bsm:hasResult IRI to ActionEffect.

Second, actor1 represents a main actor. Its column actor1 is the identifier, subject expression actor_{actor1}, class bsm:Actor. Property bsm:conceptName from actor1 (name evidence), and inter1 to bsm:typeName (description evidence: inter1 indicates type of Actor 1).

Third, actor2 similarly uses column actor2, expression actor_{actor2}, class bsm:Actor, with bsm:conceptName from actor2 and bsm:typeName from inter2.

Fourth, the location is an entity built from location and country columns, expression loc_{location}_{country}, class bsm:Location. Property bsm:locationName from location (name evidence) and bsm:hasGeometry IRI to AbsolutePoint.

Fifth, the point geometry uses same location and country keys, expression point_{location}_{country}, class bsm:AbsolutePoint, with bsm:latitudeDecimal from latitude and bsm:longitudeDecimal from longitude (name evidence).

Sixth, the fatalities outcome is an ActionEffect entity keyed by event_id_cnty, expression effect_{event_id_cnty}, class bsm:ActionEffect. Property bsm:effectQuantityNumber from fatalities (name evidence) and bsm:effectDescriptionCode constant "Fatalities" (weak evidence).

Columns with no suitable ontology match include year, time_precision, disorder_type, sub_event_type, assoc_actor_1, assoc_actor_2, interaction, civilian_targeting, iso, region, admin1, admin2, admin3, geo_precision, source, source_scale, tags, timestamp, population_1km, population_2km, population_5km, population_best.

